# Implementation Plan - Save Custom Factors

## Goal Description
Allow users to save the calculated emission factors directly to their "Custom Factor Library" (manage-data) from the specific calculator results.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> The 'Manage Data' system uses `POST /api/factors` and supports units `scf`, `m3`, `gal`.
> The Calculator produces results in various units. I will map these as follows:
> - `kg/m³` -> Unit `m3`
> - `kg/scf` -> Unit `scf`
> - `lb/gal` (converted to kg) -> Unit `gal`
> - `kg/kg` -> Not currently supported by Manage Data UI directly as a 'unit' dropdown, might need to default to a generic handling or add 'kg' support if needed. (Actually [manage-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html) only shows scf/m3/gal. I will stick to those for now or default to m3/scf/gal where applicable).

## Proposed Changes

### UI Layer
#### [MODIFY] [emission-factor.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/emission-factor.html)
- Add a "Save to Library" button in the `results-panel`.
- Implement an **inline** `save-form` div within the results panel (initially hidden).
    - Inputs: Name (Text), Unit (Select: derived from calculated results).
- Implement `toggleSaveForm(show)` function.
    - Expands/collapses the save section below the results.
- Implement `confirmSaveFactor()` function.
    - Calls `fetch('/api/factors', { method: 'POST', ... })`.
    - Shows success toast.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
1. Calculate a factor (e.g., Flaring Natural Gas).
2. Click "Save to Library".
3. Enter name "My Flare Factor". Select "m³" unit.
4. Click Save.
5. Go to "Manage Data" -> "Custom Factors" and verify "My Flare Factor" appears with correct values.
